            </Main>
            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>The infiltration test demonstrate air leakage on the following house components:

-Windows: We noticed some air leakage on the following units:

-Basement: Laundry room

-Main floor: Living room (Latches are obsolete)

-Door: We noticed air leakage around the back door. The addition of weather stripping might reduce the leakage and            increase the air tightness of the door.

-Electrical panel: We noticed air leakage around the electrical panel

-Header joist: We noticed air infiltration from the header joist floor. The addition of insulation and air seals might help to   reduce the infiltration.

</airSeal>
                <mainWalls>At the moment of the assessment the walls are made by 2x4 with an insulation level estimated of R-10. This level of insulation is far under the actual standard, we recommend the addition of insulataion to meet the city of Whitehorse standard of R-28. We recommend, to proceed from the exterior, in this way it will give the possibility to wrap the building and ensure a proper air sealing of the building. Also, by working from outside, the addition of insulation will not reduce the interior space and it will also eliminate the unpleasantness of living through renovations. </mainWalls>
                <ceilings>At the time of the inspection we observed that the roof insulation level is R-20. We recommend adding insulation to meet the actual standard based at R-60.</ceilings>
                <foundation>At the moment of the inspection, we estimated the insulation level of the basement to be as follow:

-Concrete wall: 2?????????????????? XTPS R-10 H: 3.5?????????

-Pony wall: 2x4@16??????????????????, R-10 Fiberglass batt insulation H: 4.5?????????

</foundation>
                <windows>At the moment of the inspection, we noticed a bit of leakage on windows. We recommend the reparation of the latches on the living room window or if impossible the replacement of the unit. The windows don?????????t close properly and therefore is leaky. We recommend the use of an ENERGY STAR CERTIFIED product.</windows>
                <doors>We noticed air leakage coming from the back door. The addition of weather strips might help to reduce the gap between the door and the frame. If replacement of the door, we recommend to use an ENERGY STAR CERTIFIED product.</doors>
                <VentilationSystem>With the infiltration test, we noticed that the natural ventilation in the house is not sufficient. The house showed signs of a high level of humidity. We recommend the installation of an HRV (Heat Recovery Ventilator) unit, ENERGY STAR and HVI (Home Ventilation Institute) certified.</VentilationSystem>
                <AdditionalComments>During the assessment the owner shared some concerns about the space located under the staircase. At the moment of the inspection the space is insulated, but not heated and is used as storage. During the infiltration test, we noticed air leakage around the door which cools down the room. 

-We recommend the installation of insulation behind the access door. We recommend the usage of 2?????????????????? rigid foam.

-We recommend also the installation of weather strips to seal the door when closed.

</AdditionalComments>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
